From: nfs2015-wine-cx-port <BmOdtQAYHaz36O85F8A@gcqd.fr>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:13:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tests: add the execution-breakpoint regression fixture

Standalone fixture covering both halves of this series: delivery of an x86
hardware execution breakpoint to a translated process, and the prefixed
PUSHF/POPF forms the trap-flag emulator decodes.

Ten checks. The first five are pure architecture and hold on real hardware too,
so a stock Windows run is a valid control; the last five need the breakpoint to
actually be delivered and are the ones this series fixes. Exit status is the
number of failures. Reported on the Wine 11.18 build of the same series: 2
failures with WINE_TF_EMULATION unset, 0 with
WINE_TF_EMULATION=1 WINE_TF_MAX_STEPS=0 WINE_TF_MAX_NS=0.

Kept out of dlls/ntdll/tests on purpose, as tests/nfs2015/ is not in configure's
SUBDIRS and so cannot affect a build. Converting it to a winetest case would
mean rewriting every assertion away from the form the numbers above were
measured against, and checks 6-10 would then fail any make test run on Rosetta
that did not also set WINE_TF_EMULATION=1 -- that is, the default. README.md
records the rationale, the build line and the expected results.

The .exe is not committed.
